# Source photographs. These live on disk so the cards can be re-cut at a
# different size, crop or quality, but they are not tracked: one of them is a
# 13.9-megapixel phone photo at 11.6 MB, and the page only ever loads the small
# derived copy.
#
# What IS tracked, and what the game actually loads:
#   images/loc_*.jpg          the location cards   (built by tools/make_photos.py)
#   images/cutscene_birth.jpg the birth cutscene  (ditto)
#   images/Solo_Jazz_design.jpg  the wallpaper's colour reference, kept because
#                                 it is tiny and documents where the palette came from
#
# tools/make_photos.py --check degrades gracefully when a source is absent: it
# still verifies the card exists at the right size, and says so rather than
# failing. tools/test_photos.js relies on that.
images/*.jpg
!images/loc_*.jpg
!images/cutscene_birth.jpg
!images/Solo_Jazz_design.jpg

# Python bytecode cache -- tools/ has no importable modules, but debugging
# scripts that add tools/ to sys.path will create this.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
